From: BoxDroid <boxdroid@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tcg: allow Android placement of the serial host CPU thread

Downstream status: not submitted upstream. The platform selects a measured
policy using allowed masks and reported core capacities. Invoke it once on
the actual TCG host thread before publishing startup readiness. It does not
split guest instructions, alter their ordering or change virtual clocks.
Other emulation workers retain scheduler-default placement. Unsupported or
restricted configurations preserve Android's scheduler.

diff --git a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.c b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.c
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-rr.c
@@ -177,6 +177,10 @@
  * elsewhere.
  */
 
+#ifdef BOXDROID_XBOX_RUNTIME
+extern void boxdroid_android_configure_tcg_thread(void);
+#endif
+
 static void *rr_cpu_thread_fn(void *arg)
 {
     Notifier force_rcu;
@@ -187,6 +191,11 @@
     force_rcu.notify = rr_force_rcu;
     rcu_add_force_rcu_notifier(&force_rcu);
     tcg_register_thread();
+#ifdef BOXDROID_XBOX_RUNTIME
+    /* Configure only this host CPU thread before guest execution starts.
+     * Other workers retain their original masks. Guest execution is serial. */
+    boxdroid_android_configure_tcg_thread();
+#endif
 
     bql_lock();
     qemu_thread_get_self(cpu->thread);
